        {
          "t": "h",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Stack defines vertical separation between sibling elements. It governs layout rhythm and grouping across pages and components."
        },
        {
          "t": "h",
          "level": 5,
          "text": "Token Structure"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Located in: Semantic — Size → stack.*\n\nExamples:\nstack.sm\nstack.md\nstack.lg\n\nEach stack token maps to a rem value from size / scale.\n\nExample:\nstack.md → 1rem (16px)\nstack.lg → 1.25rem (20px)\nstack.xl → 1.5rem (24px)",
          "style": "16/400"
        },
        {
          "t": "h",
          "level": 5,
          "text": "When to Use Stack"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Use stack to separate:\nSections\nContent groups\nForm fields\nLayout blocks\n\nIf two elements share the same parent and require spacing between them, use a stack token.",
          "style": "Body/Body M/Regular"
        }
      ]
    },
