        {
          "t": "h",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Inset defines internal padding within containers. It creates breathing room between content and structural boundaries."
        },
        {
          "t": "h",
          "level": 5,
          "text": "Token Structure"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Located in: Semantic — Size → inset.*\n\nExamples:\ninset.sm\ninset.md\ninset.lg\n\nEach inset token references a rem value from the sizing scale.\n\nExample:\ninset.md → 1rem (16px)\ninset.lg → 1.25rem (20px)\ninset.xl → 1.5rem (24px)",
          "style": "16/400"
        },
        {
          "t": "h",
          "level": 5,
          "text": "When to Use Inset"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Use inset inside:\nCards\nPanels\nSections\nDialogs\nPage containers\n\nInset defines containment — not separation between siblings.",
          "style": "Body/Body M/Regular"
        }
      ]
    }
